@startuml transducer-two-tape
' D2 — Transducer two-tape view.
' Depicts: a single Levenshtein-WFST transition reads an INPUT label (query side) and writes an
' OUTPUT label (dictionary side), carrying a tropical weight. The four edit operations map to the
' four labelled arcs out of a product state (dict_node, query_pos). Math typeset with <latex>.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #D6EAF8
  BorderColor #34495E
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
title D2 · The Levenshtein automaton as a two-tape transducer\ninput tape = query (misspelled)   ·   output tape = dictionary term (correction)

state "S = (dict_node, query_pos)" as S #FDEBD0
state "advance both\n(dict_node+1, query_pos+1)" as MS #D1F2EB
state "advance dict only\n(dict_node+1, query_pos)" as INS #D1F2EB
state "advance query only\n(dict_node, query_pos+1)" as DEL #D1F2EB

S -[#2ECC71]-> MS : <b>match</b>   <latex>q[i]:w[j] / 0</latex>   <latex>(q[i] = w[j])</latex>
S -[#E74C3C]-> MS : <b>substitute</b>   <latex>q[i]:w[j] / 1</latex>   <latex>(q[i] \neq w[j])</latex>
S -[#3498DB]-> INS : <b>insert</b>   <latex>\varepsilon : w[j] / 1</latex>   (extra dict char)
S -[#E67E22]-> DEL : <b>delete</b>   <latex>q[i] : \varepsilon / 1</latex>   (missing dict char)

note bottom of S
  Each arc is  <latex>\text{input} : \text{output} / \text{weight}</latex>.
  • input  = query-side label  (None = <latex>\varepsilon</latex>)
  • output = dict-side  label  (None = <latex>\varepsilon</latex>)
  • weight = TropicalWeight (0 = free match, 1 = one edit)
  A path's total weight (⊗ = +) is its edit distance.
end note
@enduml
